            <ArticleTitle>Atypical Presentation of Sjögren-Larsson Syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7981750</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2017/7981750</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sjögren-Larsson syndrome is a rare neurocutaneous disorder characterized by ichthyosis, spastic diplegia or tetraplegia, and intellectual disability. Herein, we describe a case of a Greek patient with ichthyosis and spasticity of the legs but with normal intelligence (IQ 95). This syndrome should be suspected when a child presents with ichthyosis and spastic diplegia or tetraplegia, even if intelligence is normal.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
